;; kanjō 勘定 — seed of DISCLOSED 決算 facts for SUPPLY-CHAIN CHOKEPOINT companies (primary disclosure)
;; ADR-2606032000 / ADR-0003 · vocabulary: corporate-financials-ontology.kotoba.edn
;;
;; WHY THIS FILE: the kanjō×kabuto dependency map (depgraph.cljc) surfaced the world's systemic supply
;;   chokepoints — TSMC, ASML, Arm, and the Japanese semiconductor-equipment/materials cluster — but
;;   they carried NO disclosed financials, because the live-ingest coverage is EDGAR/US-heavy. This is
;;   the non-US gap. Here we anchor those exact chokepoint nodes to their disclosed FY2024 headline
;;   figures so the world-economy dependency graph is grounded in scale where it matters most.
;;
;; SOURCING (G5): every filing + fact is :representative — publicly-documented HEADLINE annual-results
;;   figures, ROUNDED, in :millions of the filing currency. NOT line-item-exact authoritative XBRL.
;;   The authoritative path parses each filer's primary disclosure (TSMC/ASML/Arm Form 20-F via SEC
;;   EDGAR; the JP cluster via EDINET 有価証券報告書) and is G7 operator+Council gated. :company/id
;;   reuses the kabuto / tsumugi org.corp.* space (so these JOIN the supply edges by key). Absence of a
;;   company = "not yet ingested". Currency is the filing currency; NO cross-currency Σ is computed (no
;;   FX layer, R0) — KRW/CNY/SEK filers (Samsung, SK Hynix, CATL, Ericsson) are deliberately deferred
;;   until kanjō's unit set covers them, NOT because they are less critical.
;;
;; NON-ADJUDICATING (G2) / NO ADVICE (G4): these are the numbers each company itself disclosed. kanjō
;;   records them; it does NOT rate, rank "good/bad", value, or recommend any action.

